  Quote of the Week:

  Pope Julius II, in reply to Michelangelo, who had asked which of his 
artistic tools the Pope would like to try (1506):
  "Nay, give me a sword, for I am no scholar."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  A diplomatic furor erupted between the Realms of Neferititi (#2) (whose 
alliances are too incompatible) and Xin II, degrading their diplomatic 
relations 1 level(s)!
  Thus endeth the adventures of Xin II for this year.



  Here is the financial report for Xin II's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 0 gold in revenue.  0 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  0 
gold was expended to maintain our armies.  Xin II was left with 3 gold in 
the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Moosu, Squire to Belleus
To: Xin II

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the advent of the spring season Belleus prepared to quench his thirst 
for glory.  He prepared his armies to defend Hong Kong and the surrounding 
provinces.

  Thy humble servant,   Moosu, Squire to Belleus


From: Gordius
To: Xin II

  Honored Sovereign, 

  Frigid winter melted into fragrant spring, and I made ready to carry out 
my urgent assignments.  I prepared my armies to defend Ulan Bator and the 
surrounding provinces.

  Thy humble servant,   Gordius


